# Defect 507's class, 2026-10-08, and panel 199's R3, ratified 2026-10-09:
# the spec-warden's `hidden2`, a correct program whose recursion ends on an
# `exit` inside a callee that otherwise returns. clang cannot see that the
# call may not return, and said *all paths through this function will call
# itself [-Winfinite-recursion]* at every level, false, where no mark on the
# emitted `exit` reaches (lane b15-emit's repair left it standing). Panel
# 199's R1 spares the function (reading R4: the callee may end the program),
# and since R3 clang's warning is not passed on (`-Wno-infinite-recursion`,
# `selfhost/cli/flags.hero`), the checker the witness of what it could tell.
# It prints 1, 2 and 3 and exits 0 at every level; the `warnings` suite holds
# its build to no clang warning, which it gave before.
function next(n: i64) -> i64
    return n + 1

function stop_after(n: i64)
    if n > 3
        exit(code: 0)

function serve(n: i64) -> i64
    stop_after(n)
    print(n)
    return serve(next(n))

function main()
    print(serve(1))
